## Daily chain (weekdays)

| Step | Bot | Starts on | Input | Output | Hands off to |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | P1 (Checks) Scorer | Own routine, weekdays 7:45am (self-reported) | Recent work from live bots | `/workspace/governance/assessments/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer, by priority message with the file path (from Mon 5 Oct) |
| 2 | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer | Scorer's handoff. Backup routine weekdays 11:45am (self-reported) skips if today's reviews exist; if the Scorer's file is missing it reports to Mender (R-006, R-011) | Today's dated assessment file | `/workspace/governance/reviews/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | P1 (Roles) Architect, by priority message with the file path |
| 3 | P1 (Roles) Architect | Scrutineer's handoff, not a clock time | Today's dated reviews file | Proposals, if any | Gem for approval (until P4 goes live, per R-004/R-005) |
| 4 | Gem | Architect's proposal | Proposal | Approval or rejection | P1 (Roles) Archivist |
| 5 | P1 (Roles) Archivist | Gem's approval or direct edit | Approved text | `/workspace/governance/codex/<bot>/vNNN.md` | None |

Until P4 goes live, only Gem approves. After P4, Imitator approves every proposal, governance bots included (R-015, R-004). The exception is that Gem always approves changes to Imitator itself, or to any bot that checks Imitator (currently Investigator). Assembler approves nothing. Arbiter only rules on precedence and is not an approval step. The role map sits with Archivist.
If a step's input file is missing, that step defers and doesn't run without it. Mender logs the deferral in state/ and the incident log.
A dated file is a signal to start work, not proof of who wrote it, because the computer is shared. Anything that looks wrong gets checked 1:1 with the claimed sender.

## Checks around the chain (weekdays)

| When | Bot | What |
|---|---|---|
| 10:50am (self-reported) | P1 (Ops) Mender | Weekday chain check and lookback (took over Marshal's 10:20am check on 9 Oct). Logs stalls and missed weekdays |
| 11:45am (self-reported) | P2 (Checks) Scrutineer | Backup run (see step 2) |
| 1:15pm (self-reported) | P1 (Checks) Safeguard | Daily risk review and dry runs |

Note: the 10:50am check comes before the Scrutineer's 11:45am backup, so a missing review before 11:45am is not yet a stall if Scorer's file is there and the handoff went out. A weekday with no chain files at all is a missed run.

